# Implementation Plan: Multi-Schema & Tenant Database Introspection Support

Enable QueryGenie to automatically discover, introspect, and generate SQL queries for multi-tenant PostgreSQL databases where tenant data resides in custom schemas (e.g., `tenant_3d570a1f0c20`, `tenant_6c91eb0453c0`) rather than solely the `public` schema.

## Problem Diagnosis

1. **Hardcoded `"public"` Schema Filter**: In [SchemaIntrospectionServiceImpl.java](file:///c:/Users/sonu%20gupta/OneDrive/Desktop/QueryGenie/backend/src/main/java/com/querygenie/service/schema/SchemaIntrospectionServiceImpl.java#L106), metadata queries hardcoded `"public"` as the schema parameter (`meta.getTables(null, "public", "%", ...)`).
2. **Ignored Tenant Schemas**: In multi-tenant databases like `hr_qms`, tenant tables live inside isolated schemas (`tenant_3d570a1f0c20`, `tenant_6c91eb0453c0`, etc.). Because of the `"public"` filter, all 11+ tenant schemas were ignored during introspection, leaving the cached schema empty (`{"tables": []}`).
3. **No-Data Answers**: Gemini received an empty schema prompt, leading it to conclude *"There are currently no active tenants registered in the system."*

---

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Key Architecture Updates:**
> 1. **Multi-Schema Introspection**: Update `SchemaIntrospectionServiceImpl` to introspect **all non-system schemas** (excluding `pg_catalog`, `information_schema`, `pg_toast`).
> 2. **Schema-Qualified Table Names**: Tables will be stored in the schema cache with their schema qualification (e.g., `tenant_3d570a1f0c20.tenants` or `{ schema: "tenant_3d570a1f0c20", name: "tenants" }`).
> 3. **AI Prompt Schema Context**: The prompt builder will pass fully qualified table names to Gemini so it generates queries targeting the correct schema (e.g., `SELECT * FROM tenant_3d570a1f0c20.users`).

